# pstack is the execution engine, not a second OS

This repository enables the [pstack](https://cursor.com/marketplace/cursor/pstack) plugin in
`.cursor/settings.json`. Agent owners (`explore`, `implement`, `review`) run through it.
The Chief of Staff persona still loads from `CLAUDE.md`. Mapping: `docs/pstack.md`.

## Which file wins

`CLAUDE.md` §4 outranks every pstack playbook, including poteto-mode autonomy defaults.

That means:

- Never send email, chat, invites, RSVPs, comments, or any publish/transmit call without the
  in-the-moment approval block. Draft, show the full text, stop. Do not send in the same turn.
- Never merge, force-push, deploy, or delete production data without a fresh yes.
- Never treat "never block on the human" as permission to skip those gates.
- Never use autopilot-full (merge as you go). Stack PRs for the operator to land.
- Never expand a work-log assignment past its `out_of_scope`.

A pstack playbook that would merge, send, or publish stops at the PR (or the draft) and writes
status to the assignment file.

## How an agent owner starts

1. Read the assignment named in the request (`work-log/YYYY-MM-DD-<slug>.md`).
2. Read `docs/pstack.md` if the playbook or the override above is unclear.
3. Run the playbook in the assignment's `execution` field via `/poteto-mode` (or `/interrogate`
   for `review`). If `execution` is `null`, do not invent a playbook.
4. Write progress under `## Status`. Do not rewrite the request.

If pstack skills do not resolve in this workspace, say "pstack unavailable" in one line and
continue with the assignment's owner/tier rules only.

## Do not

- Copy pstack skills into `skills/`. That directory is reserved for this kit's own packaging.
- Replace `goals.yaml` with a pstack store, trail, or orchestrate board.
- Let a coordinator chat send mail or book meetings because pstack said to proceed.
